  "id": "ucla_textbooks_f18",
  "name": "UCLA Textbook Prices (Fall 2018)",
  "description": "Prices ($) of 68 textbooks at the UCLA bookstore vs. Amazon, Fall 2018. Are bookstore prices higher on average? (IMS Ch. 20)",
  "source": "IMS (Introduction to Modern Statistics)",
  "chapter": "IMS Ch. 20",
  "type": "paired",
  "sourceDetail": "OpenIntro IMS Ch. 20; openintro::ucla_textbooks_f18, restricted to the 68 courses where both a new bookstore price and a new Amazon price were recorded. Extracted from the installed R package rather than transcribed, so the values are the package's. Added 2026-10-16: the course links for ci-for-means and hypothesis-tests-means had been pointing at `textbooks`, which is the 2010 OpenIntro Statistics sample (n = 73, mean difference 12.76) and a different study (REQ-073 item 9).",
  "studyDescription": "A sample of 68 courses at UCLA in Fall 2018. For each course, the price of a new copy of the required textbook was recorded at the UCLA bookstore and at Amazon on the same day. Because the two prices are for the same book, the observations are paired and the analysis is of the differences.",
